-- Backfill reflection for the 68 'non-skills-videos' rows.
-- Generated by scripts/generate-reflections-migration.py from scripts/data/reflections/non-skills-videos.json.
-- Targets rows by stable id. Fails the transaction if the expected row
-- count is not updated.

do $$
declare
  expected_count int := 68;
  actual_count int;
begin
  with v(id, new_reflection) as (values
      ('0461e1f0-9319-49cb-b998-a2d40146d6f2', 'Some breakthroughs take decades and quiet careers. As you think about how you measure a working life, would you want one big visible win, or a long contribution to something most people will never know your name for?'),
      ('04a7514a-6ba4-4584-88c3-b92b3ab4e460', 'Some careers depend on connecting systems that look unrelated. As you think about your own way of seeing the world, do you naturally look for what links things, or do you find yourself focusing on one piece at a time?'),
      ('06ddf92e-580f-4fcb-ab3b-017fe71bf562', 'Some financial myths cost people money for years. As you think about your own future earnings, what is one money belief you grew up with that you would actually want to test before you let it shape your decisions?'),
      ('0b91f634-5412-4deb-a5a5-6837782a2c48', 'Some jobs ask you to be right the first time, every time. As you think about your own appetite for high-stakes precision, would you welcome a role where the math has to be perfect, or would you find it crushing over years?'),
      ('107d56b9-4cb7-47fc-b277-10ec9067a504', 'Some careers are forming at the overlap of fields most people never see overlap. As you think about your own interests, where do two of your curiosities cross, and would you bet on the intersection becoming a real career?'),
      ('1435a814-a480-4f66-b62c-2748a22f3cbd', 'Some hiring red flags are easy to miss when you want the job badly. As you think about your own next job search, what would help you slow down enough to notice when something is off, before you give away time or information?'),
      ('190bb7d5-ab11-4cb1-b1e5-8068a28b8cd7', 'Some careers piece together survival rules from the past. As you think about what catches your attention, are you drawn to stories about how things ended, or about how they survived against the odds?'),
      ('1adf0549-4096-45c3-a97c-47911127a057', 'Some jobs exist to transform how someone feels. As you think about your own ambition, would you find meaning in work that changes how a person sees themselves, even if the role does not have a familiar career title attached to it?'),
      ('1fc5b5a4-ae24-4236-a651-55de7c6b658d', 'A clear interest at fifteen does not have to wait for graduation. As you think about something you are already drawn to, what is one real, low-cost way you could start building on it before you finish high school?'),
      ('23e374ad-8591-4ba4-8a8d-8ebc164a31d6', 'Specific beats enthusiastic in interviews. As you think about a workplace you might apply to, what could you find out in one hour of research that would let you answer this question better than ninety percent of other candidates?'),
      ('29d97e13-6d0a-4d14-8850-42174e900ac4', 'Some careers turn rare cases into new standards. As you think about your own values, would you rather work on solutions that help many people a little, or solutions that change one life entirely?'),
      ('2e772d92-e0be-4476-8a61-af8c2239c366', 'Some careers sit behind ordinary-looking phenomena. As you think about what catches your attention, are you the kind of person who wants to know why something looks the way it does, even when the question seems small?'),
      ('30f6aff8-fa3e-4f69-af73-de29f6f7ef2e', 'Knowing what is off-limits in an interview is part of professional fluency. As you imagine your own first real interview, how would you decline a question while staying in the running for the role?'),
      ('32307240-5731-40b1-b146-0eb970f00d96', 'First jobs are usually about proving you can handle people, pressure, and routine. As you think about your own first job, what would change if you treated it as training for everything that comes after, instead of just income?'),
      ('37b0859e-e5c5-4970-90bf-9a9ea88bd906', 'The world is full of careers you have never heard of. As you think about your own future, are you genuinely curious about jobs outside your immediate world, or do you mostly look at the ones already in front of you?'),
      ('383ae2ac-b671-448b-8b51-32f036929a52', 'Side jobs are how people test new directions without quitting their day job. As you think about something you are curious about, could you build a small version of it on the side before committing fully?'),
      ('38d01073-4666-41af-bf77-d5e36783d84a', 'Some scientists study extreme environments to reshape other fields. As you think about your own curiosity, would you commit years to a place or organism most people will never see, if the work might quietly affect medicine or materials?'),
      ('3b2db940-8f3d-4108-b896-cbbbc7904a5e', 'Workplace generational gaps are big enough to support a whole career. As you think about your own first job, what would you want a boss to understand about your generation, and what would you need to understand about theirs?'),
      ('3b54102e-a5a4-4fce-b8b9-187bcebb9c39', 'Some careers blend science with logistics most people cannot picture. As you think about your own appetite for difficulty, would you welcome a job where the environment is part of the challenge, or would you want easier conditions to focus?'),
      ('3d82a2c0-31b6-43fa-83e7-ee036ea9147e', 'Some careers turn small molecular issues into global safety solutions. As you think about your own attention, are you drawn to small details that quietly affect a lot of people, or to big problems with obvious stakes?'),
      ('3e54daf8-d84f-43d5-b03c-31df7274aa2b', 'Some careers grow out of a hobby or natural ability. As you think about something you do without much effort, who would pay you for it if it kept getting better over years, and would you want them to?'),
      ('3e5aec5f-3b1f-4b40-8d8e-05655b84f57c', 'Peer recognition often opens doors grades cannot. As you think about your own time in school, what is one specific thing you have already become known for, and could that become a story you reuse on applications?'),
      ('3eaca167-50b8-4f09-965b-2cd95c858095', 'If your manager does not know what you did, it did not happen. As you think about your own work style, are you comfortable telling people about your wins, or does that feel like crossing a line for you?'),
      ('417dd831-6c42-40fc-be70-1ae997ee8ac0', 'Career and financial independence are about options, not just income. As you think about your own future, what is one financial habit you would want in place before you really need it?'),
      ('42bf77a5-576a-46ef-967d-56450d199a89', 'Some careers were not options twenty years ago. As you think about your own next decade, what would change if you picked a field that did not exist when your parents finished school, knowing it might be normal by the time you finish?'),
      ('434e6ce6-1d08-4e05-87ae-e2a6e5188ebd', 'Breaking into a field is one challenge; staying long enough to do it twice is another. As you imagine your own career, where would you want your persistence to show, even when an easier exit is available?'),
      ('4db2c063-e97b-411f-9444-afcd984dd7b1', 'Some of the most lucrative careers are not on any school career-fair list. As you think about how you find career ideas, where do you look beyond the obvious sources, and who could you ask?'),
      ('4e8afc40-e019-4dda-8189-f60a9e31d2b1', 'Bad work experiences leave residue in the next role. As you imagine your own first hard job, what would help you not bring it into the next one with you?'),
      ('5bee58d6-fd91-4e3a-8761-90bd24afc9d3', 'Some research is reshaping how we define intelligence. As you think about your own definition of what counts as smart, would you welcome a job that asks you to question that assumption every day?'),
      ('5c311d08-ea00-4832-a4ce-5320c09974d9', 'Some technologies are moving from physics labs into commercial products. As you think about your own appetite for early-stage work, would you join a field where the use cases are still being invented, or one where the playbook is settled?'),
      ('5c3ba7fb-b56b-439b-a6a1-2840e4b6277b', 'Some careers engineer who sits where and why. As you think about your own way of solving problems, do you focus on the equipment, on the people, or on how the two interact?'),
      ('5d445aca-db3c-4695-b0cc-6f5e4addb792', 'Structured stories beat vague claims in interviews. As you think about your own experiences, what are two or three moments you could turn into a flexible story that fits many future questions?'),
      ('6a79c7fb-bf45-4e7d-81a3-25e7feeaa443', 'Some careers turn a single experiment into measurable outcomes for patients. As you think about your own appetite for slow work, would you spend years on one trial knowing it might help thousands, or would that feel too distant from impact?'),
      ('735320ff-3ed7-4600-80fa-67bd6cb553c3', 'Some careers chase rare events that bend the whole work around them. As you think about your own pace, would you welcome a job where most of the time is preparation, and a few moments are the entire point?'),
      ('745e58d1-d7f2-4af7-84d2-51a6900e1699', 'Some early-career researchers get to define what is possible. As you think about your own future, would you join a field where the basic questions are still open, or one where the work is already well established?'),
      ('75588039-9ecf-4e2a-97c5-4db970e26c94', 'Job hunting now means screening employers as carefully as they screen you. As you think about your own appetite for caution, where in the application process would you slow down to verify that an opportunity is real?'),
      ('75ee354d-4459-4799-889d-9a85534b07c2', 'Most famous people are not household names. As you think about your own ambition, would you rather be widely known for one thing, or quietly known by the right small group of people for a craft you take seriously?'),
      ('81874841-de33-4fed-8799-4f6852cbb74c', 'Some scientists work on questions whose answers may not arrive in their lifetime. As you think about your own appetite for unfinished work, can you find satisfaction in adding a piece to a question someone else will eventually finish?'),
      ('81ed251d-efa5-4083-9ce1-1bdf4c1aadca', 'Some fields are still discovering new species. As you think about your own curiosity, where would you go if you wanted to work in a part of science where the unknown is still that big?'),
      ('8874e2a1-9883-4eae-8279-e8a586c1912c', 'Some careers design for how people actually feel, not just how things work. As you think about your own way of solving problems, would you want a job that ends with a number, or one that ends with someone feeling differently than they did before?'),
      ('942fa90c-12a3-40cb-a168-6fd2a5dc535e', 'Some careers reorient around rare events when they appear. As you think about your own way of working, would you welcome a job where your entire year could shift because of one unusual signal in the sky?'),
      ('94c97e4f-ce4b-4e5b-9ba0-0309ce7112d1', 'Some sciences are becoming chemistry and imaging fields as much as their original ones. As you think about a field you are drawn to, would you welcome learning two disciplines at once, or would you rather pick one and go deep?'),
      ('993640e7-922a-468e-a5c2-6b98e4fb1b47', 'Reneging on an accepted offer is rare but sometimes the right call. As you think about your own integrity, can you imagine doing it professionally if the right opportunity arrived one week too late?'),
      ('9cdf9b1a-2d15-4f42-826b-d825898ee6ae', 'Salary transparency is one of the fastest ways to find out if you are underpaid. As you imagine your own first job, would you discuss pay openly with coworkers, or would that still feel like crossing a line?'),
      ('9fd16bb6-708e-4edf-8b85-4517402b12ce', 'Some jobs touching tradition, culture, and the arts do not advertise themselves. As you think about a world you are curious about, who could you ask about the kinds of jobs that live inside it but stay invisible from outside?'),
      ('a1bd666e-d6a3-44ed-b644-7bad37bdcc70', 'Most candidates do not lose offers on answers; they lose them on the small habits around the conversation. As you think about your own attention, would you remember the follow-up email, the eye contact, the post-interview silence?'),
      ('a1fc5166-94a0-4484-a136-333174fedf4d', 'Career growth is not always vertical. As you think about your own future, can you imagine turning down a promotion if the new role would not actually suit you, even when the title and pay are better?'),
      ('b3dda504-e1d3-494a-886d-dbadeb9860ac', 'Benefits only matter if you can actually take them. As you think about your own future job hunt, what would you ask in an interview to find out whether a perk is real or only theoretical?'),
      ('b4eb7806-0a03-4267-bca1-f7069d3e4e84', 'Some careers study extremes to imagine life elsewhere. As you think about your own curiosity, are you more interested in what is true here, or in what those same patterns might mean for places we have not been yet?'),
      ('b9a40c94-0a27-4a9c-a607-c2b8a84fd507', 'Career experience can start before you can drive. As you think about your own age, what is one thing you could try this year that would put you ahead of where you would otherwise be at twenty?'),
      ('baf1b86e-383a-47e0-99d6-1b1420688c42', 'Small talk is how trust gets built before the real conversation starts. As you think about your own social energy, do you find casual talk draining or interesting, and what would it take to lean into it on purpose?'),
      ('beab524b-fb4a-4b06-9e28-4776c095592d', 'Some career playbooks are being written right now by the people who chose them. As you think about your own future, would you join a field where the standards are already set, or one where someone like you will define them?'),
      ('c0702611-7a92-474c-9984-f9714ff42f95', 'Staying neutral early in a career protects your reputation. As you think about your own habits, are you the kind of person who shares opinions easily, or do you wait to see how a situation unfolds before weighing in?'),
      ('ca576729-2cb7-4c93-a090-a4c73422b8e5', 'Some careers ask all of you at once: physical, mental, emotional. As you think about your own capacity, do you have a setting where you can carry hard things and recover, or do you tend to bring stress home with you?'),
      ('cd1c3fca-7410-47db-9cdd-55d75e969079', 'Workplace norms are less fixed than they look. As you think about your own first real job, when would you speak up about something that does not feel right, and when would you let it slide to keep the peace?'),
      ('ce24edef-9783-4451-a3ec-c1d508182063', 'Loving what you do and earning well are not mutually exclusive. As you imagine your own career, where would you look for the third category most people never search for: passionate, paid, and possible?'),
      ('ce2a7e74-fee6-490d-8b25-adfb021db0b7', 'Some careers are so specialized they do not appear in any database. As you think about your own curiosity, what is one rabbit hole that has held your attention longer than most, and where could that take you?'),
      ('cee339f6-df02-4d20-abab-993d2092f946', 'Boundaries are how high performers protect the time they need. As you think about your own habits, do you say yes too easily, and what would change if you treated boundaries as part of doing good work?'),
      ('d4eb3a3b-1723-4f1c-b16f-4cc17d7ff345', 'Time, not income, is the biggest lever in long-term saving. As you think about your own future, what would it change to start now with a small amount, instead of waiting until you earn more?'),
      ('da3ae5d7-ebac-4973-bd68-9786282c68de', 'Most workplace arguments are won by making the other person feel heard. As you think about your own communication style, do you reach for logic first, or do you start by acknowledging the other side?'),
      ('dd48c8cd-f0c0-40b4-ba87-6b8f97a2a399', 'The first sixty seconds after a job offer set the tone for your compensation. As you imagine your own first offer, what would you want yourself to say to keep the door open for negotiation?'),
      ('de3b6239-5e36-4dfd-805c-efc3dc427128', 'Whole industries exist around appearance, with paths from technician to artist. As you think about a field that interests you, would you start technical and grow into artistry, or the other way around?'),
      ('e2e1a04d-d03e-4f1d-8081-d968c5c10fec', 'Asking for more money is a normal business conversation, not a confrontation. As you think about your own comfort, does negotiation feel like advocacy for yourself, or like asking for something you do not deserve?'),
      ('f2311ce0-cbc5-4017-b840-ba2c6b2f0a51', 'Some of the most fulfilling careers are ones kids get visibly excited about. As you think about the work you might do, would you choose a job that energizes other people, even when it tires you out?'),
      ('f7267e39-9626-45bf-9e12-25d772bed8f8', 'Trick interview questions usually test composure, not knowledge. As you think about your own response under pressure, what would help you buy a beat to think before answering, instead of rushing to fill silence?'),
      ('f9e7057d-3cbf-411b-8815-374c2a641348', 'The moment between offer and acceptance is the highest leverage you will ever have. As you imagine your own first negotiation, what kind of preparation would let you ask for more without feeling awkward?'),
      ('fb96f61e-6b96-42ac-b9e9-83d683d06c7e', 'Some careers reward patience that does not look impressive day-to-day. As you think about your own attention span, can you commit to years of slow progress on something, or do you need visible wins to stay engaged?'),
      ('fc383824-a9e7-4c51-80ed-0f7c1ba6dd50', 'Some careers count things that shape big decisions. As you think about your own preferences, would you welcome a job where your work is invisible at the surface, but quietly underneath public health, economics, or policy?')
  )
  update public.content c
  set reflection = v.new_reflection
  from v
  where c.id = v.id;

  get diagnostics actual_count = row_count;
  if actual_count <> expected_count then
    raise exception 'Expected % rows updated, got %', expected_count, actual_count;
  end if;
end $$;
